- pays for itself, with no new R&D;
- volumes first: S1 is the record, and the Ducted beats a cancel in all three columns without assuming any selection;
- no overcapitalisation: about $1.0B a year against about $2.5B of room;
- premium $0;
- terms: no price talk, and standard joint terms on both invitations.
I took three things from him:
(1) His correction that a Ducted cancel saves $2.67B on the board, not $0.67B, because the strain goes with it. The row still loses $16.86-17.65B.
(2) His booking of -77 (the equal-weight value, rounded down) in place of my -75. It's the 'guide low, then raise' discipline [CX-0270, CX-0654]. We raise to S1 when the 2045 bulletin shows the codes locked.
(3) His terms conditions on the airframers' invitations and his warning that the grid's CFM volume falls to 1,270 a year from 2040, so no facility build. He would put S1 at .60; I keep .50, which he calls the right side to err on. His slip costing ($1.18B for the first year, $3.34B to 2040) goes to the Board with Ali's review.

